+/*
+ * Semantics derived from the ESP32-S3 TRM chapter "Interrupt Matrix
+ * (INTERRUPT)" (§9.3.2, §9.3.3) and the IDF S3 register headers
+ * (components/soc/esp32s3/register/soc/interrupt_core{0,1}_reg.h):
+ *
+ *  - Each CPU owns a register file of one 5-bit MAP register per peripheral
+ *    interrupt source (CPU0 at +0x000, CPU1 at +0x800).  The MAP value is the
+ *    CPU interrupt number the source is routed to.
+ *  - Multiple sources may be routed to the same CPU interrupt; the CPU
+ *    interrupt output reflects the logical OR of the asserted sources routed
+ *    to it (TRM §9.3.3.2).  A shared line only deasserts once every mapped
+ *    source has deasserted.
+ *  - Values naming a CPU *internal* interrupt (6, 7, 11, 15, 16, 29 — timer,
+ *    software and profiling interrupts, TRM Table 9.3-2) route nowhere: the
+ *    matrix only drives the 26 external CPU interrupts.  IDF uses value 6
+ *    (INT_MUX_DISABLED_INTNO) to detach a source (TRM §9.3.3.3).
+ *  - The reset value of every MAP register is 0x10 per the IDF register
+ *    header defaults; 0x10 is likewise an internal interrupt, so nothing is
+ *    routed until software programs the matrix.
+ *  - INTR_STATUS_0..3 (RO) report the current asserted level of each source,
+ *    CLOCK_GATE controls the matrix functional clock (reset: enabled), and
+ *    DATE is the version register (reset: 0x02012300).
+ *
+ * Model: the raw input level of every source is tracked independently of the
+ * map.  Each CPU's external interrupt outputs are recomputed as the OR of
+ * asserted inputs whose MAP entry selects that output, on every input edge
+ * and every map write.  A clock-gated CPU file freezes: writes are ignored,
+ * INTR_STATUS and the outputs hold their values until the clock is
+ * re-enabled, at which point the current input levels propagate.
+ */
 
 #define IRQ_MAP(cpu, input) s->irq_map[cpu][input]
 
